Z||000000||GodSend||09-20-2001||03:11 PM||||or rather, what is behind it.<P>I am interested in knowning (before I take it apart to look) what is behind the "glove box" infront of the pass. seat.  I know there is a speaker (obviously).  but what kind of room is behind there? Any electonics or anything.<P>My other question is regarding removing the "glovebox".  When I remove this item, and I expect to see a hole in the dash where is was, or is there another layer or dash material behind it? (any tips on removing it?) Thanks guys - this is for a "special project"  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> - Pics to follow soon.||||reg||1
Z||000001||MinnGreenGT||09-20-2001||03:48 PM||||I'm thinking something along the same lines... removing the box should be easy. I believe that there are 4 nuts on the back side, holding it to the assembly.  There should be material most of the way behind, by maybe not all (haven't had mine apart in ages).  <P>I'm thinking a small LCD TV would be cool in there!  (Then my PSone system and/or a portable DVD player for road trips!)  I'd just have to make a sliding door(s) to cover it when not in use!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngtsig3.jpg">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/halfpole.gif">  <BR>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett||||reg||1
Z||000002||Rodrv6||09-20-2001||04:40 PM||||The dash is solid behind the storage pocket.  There is an air duct directly behind the dash (actually bolted to it) that delivers air to the vents by the doors.  Behind that on the passenger side is the heater box.  Not a lot of excess room.<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  84 SE, 330,000 miles and counting, 88 GT, not nearly as many miles :)||||reg||1
Z||000003||StuGood||09-20-2001||06:26 PM||||If I remember, the easiest way to see what's back there, is to remove the radio speaker.  Gently pry up on the corners of the speaker grill until it comes out, and set it aside.  From there, you can remove the speaker (7mm nut driver, I think) and look inside the back of the dash through the speaker hole.<P>Might even be able to test-fit your project through the speaker hole.<P> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||GodSend||09-20-2001||07:17 PM||||minn,<P>What are you, some kind of mind reader? Actually my idea is slightly different.  I want to mound an lcd screen where the glove box is.<P>In addition I also want to run a PSOne (the newer smaller version) from it.  My idea was to actually mount it where the speaker is, and attach the speaker grill to the top of the PSone where the cd goes in.  Totally stealth, untill you push down on the grill a little bit and up pops the cover, with the place to stick the cd.<P><BR>I plan on running those controller cable extensions and allowing controllers to be plugged in via the ash tray area.  Should look good.  LCD is on the way  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I am not afraid to hack up the dash a little bit under where the glove box goes back on.  I will be putting that back in when I sell the car.. or.. IF i ever sell the car  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">.  Perhaps I can use that area (although if there is heater sutff there) to store a few cds.... good idea!<P>I am planning on doing this very soon, project should be completed in a few weeks total.  I am also going to mod the PS to play VCDs and MP3s.. which will be nice.. <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.hypernetcommunications.com/revn.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||FieroBUZZ||09-20-2001||09:28 PM||||This is the dash from the back (pass side).  The yellow cicle is around the duct to the side vent.  The red cicle around the hole which meets the heater mounted on the 'firewall'.  You could cut and seal the duct at the box.  I will be using a smaller tube and round vent. Hopefully the tube can be run around obstructions.<BR>Gary<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/dash_4.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Cheever3000||09-20-2001||11:57 PM||||Isn't anybody going to put a 'puter screen in there, so you can have the Forum up WHILE you're in your Fiero?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||GodSend||09-21-2001||12:37 AM||||Well, even though its only a 4' LCD screen I am modding my PSone to play VCD'S.  I origionally contemplated a PS2 but the cost is too great, it does not have a car adapter available, and the current draw is 3 times greater.  In addition, the PS2 (or so I hear) has a hard time reading alot of DVDS.<P>So I plan on buying a few VCDs (to start) and downloading and burning the rest. Should be a fun little project.  Total cost should be under $550 bones Canadian .. including the brand new Psone, Lcd Screen, VCD Mod, extra controllers, extensions, 12v adapter. and PPI  Par 225 in dash Eq with Aux.||||reg||1
