Z||000011||falconhulk||09-21-2001||09:44 AM||||VCD is a format popular for video pirates.  Asisa is the main place to buy VCD's.  Most new DVD players and old high end ones (mine was $700 3 years ago and it plays them)play them now.  You can make VCD's from any mpeg video.  Most burning apps let you make them now such as Nero and Easy CD creator.  If you need any more info i am somewhat of an expert at this subject just send me a PM. I removed my dash pocket and installed brackets to hold a laptop.  I use the lapto for navigation via a portable GPS and mapping software as well as to play CD's and Mp3's through the stock stereo.  I plan to upgrade to a laptop with DVD in the future. <p>[This message has been edited by falconhulk (edited 09-21-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000012||MinnGreenGT||09-21-2001||11:03 AM||||GodSend... Where'd you get your LCD?  I've been watching them on ebay and you can pick one up for around $100.  I'm considering going to the 5", but don't know if it's worth the extra cash.  Once you remove the Glove box, there will be plenty of room for the LCD- they're very slim.<P>I don't have the funds right now to work on the project, but take lots of pics when you're working on it and let me know how it goes- I can't wait!||||reg||1
Z||000013||GodSend||09-21-2001||11:05 AM|||| <A HREF="http://www.partsexpress.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.parts-express.com</A>  has a 4' video module for 109.00 bucks.<P>Basically I went the VCD route because the ease of burning them (er.... to back up mine of course!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">.  <P>The quality is not as good as DVD by a long shot, but if you get a legit VCD it is definatly better then VCR quality (you can get some pretty crappy ones though that are basically some guy setting up a camcorder aimed at a TV... :P ).<P>There are few different products that will allow you to play VCD's on your playstation.  Because I am going with a PSone system (the smaller one) I have to purchase a internal card that I have to solder at a few points (no biggie).  The old playstations have a port on the back that you plug an external little box into, which means you dont have to open the case.  <P>Anyhoots, I ordered the matrix, terminator 2, Ace Ventura 1 & 2 and Starwars 1 last night, so hopefully I will have VCD in the fiero by early next month.<P>Just do you know, I will answer a few questions<P>VCD - VideoCd , most of which has already been explained.<P>PSone - There are 2 versions of the OLDER playstation.  The origional one, which was about 75% the size of a normal box of cerial, and a PSone, which was released about a year ago, which is much smaller (about 1/3 the size).  The PSone however does not have an external port on the back, so "Mods" have to be done internally (although you can mod a psone to add the port).<P>- LCD screens typically have a RCA input on them.  <P>- There are more then a few ways to get video/audio into your fiero - here are a few.<P>a]  Get a stereo which has TV controls.  Unfortuantly, you also need to get a seperate TV TUNER which is made specifically by the company (IE - I need a Clarion TTX7001 tv tuner - $500 bones).  With this setup you get basic tv reception, but it is much easier to add in extra components (vcrs, extra tvs, video games.. and so on).  The audio runs from your source (stereo, vcr, playstation) and into your amplifiers<P>---OR -- the route I am going<P>b]  Purchase a in dash EQ (higher end versions will impove your sound system as well) that has SWITCHABLE main/aux inputs.  Basically the main input is from your stereo, and the AUX input is from your videogame (or if you have multiple add ones, then it comes from the switcher). The video is feed straight from the playstation into the LCD screen via the same rca style plugs you would use at home.  <P>-- OR ---<P>c]  You can get after market units with FMModulators.  Basically this is a self contained unit which will broadcast the audio to your radio (on a certain channel).  By far the easiest (the actual cost is very close to option b) but the sound quality is only as good as your fm radio.  If you have a nice deck, this may not be an issue at all.<P><BR>Enjoy.<p>[This message has been edited by GodSend (edited 09-21-2001).]||||reg||1
